{
  "abstract": "Relations among affine output maps can invalidate deep independence assumptions in local capacity arguments for periodic graph supports. We replace the affine action by two explicit rational Möbius transformations generating a free group. Exterior-domain and algebraic criteria separate entire polynomial branch orbits, establishing independent symmetric-group root counts at every prescribed finite depth. For the three outputs $Q,A(Q),B(Q)$, we determine the sharp asymptotic row/column relaxation capacities for $Q=X^3-3X$, $X^4-X$, and $X^5-X$: respectively $1.789191831376919\\ldots$, $1.802335973378451\\ldots$, and $1.798584319949732\\ldots$. We obtain the matching limits by verifying the hypotheses of a bipartite allocation theorem, specializing its objective, and proving uniqueness of the relevant scalar solutions. Independent matching and marked-tree energy derivations check the constants and normalization. The quartic passes the $1.8$ coordinate threshold. A uniform twelve-round certificate excludes every fixed symmetric-monodromy degree at least five with separated branch orbits at coefficient $1.7998$, making the quartic exception explicit. Eight-round covers also give explicit uniform bounds $1.789245+O(p^{-1/2}\\log p)$ and $1.799775+O(p^{-1/2}\\log p)$ for cubic and quintic selections in every translated square of side $N\\ge p$. Exact certificates and 864 physical-window checks accompany the proofs. Sharpness holds for the coordinate relaxation in complete windows of at least two periods. The relaxed point sets need not satisfy oblique-line constraints, and no unrestricted no-three construction or upper bound is claimed.",
